<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan auctions 50 mln rupees' six-month bonds.</title>
<headline>Pakistan auctions 50 mln rupees' six-month bonds.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The State (central) Bank of Pakistan said it had auctioned short-term federal bonds worth 50 million rupees in an open market operation on Thursday.</p>
<p>It said bids worth 50 million rupees were accepted for the outright sale of the six-month bonds at a maximum cut off of 16.75 percent a year.</p>
<p>In the previous auction held on January 29, the central bank accepted bids worth 400 million rupees for five-month repurchase contract of the bonds at a maximum cut-off of 16.50 percent.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
